{#
  The source of truth for every guideline export (Stage 03 PRD §12.1, §14).

  Rules for editing this file — the same four `plan.md.j2` carries, because it
  is the same job one stage later:
  - Never put a judgement in here. The template arranges what 3.6.1 and 3.6.2
    already decided; a conditional that changes a status is a node change
    wearing a template's clothes.
  - Every long table states its own cap in the document. A claims table
    silently cut to 50 rows reads as a complete register, and a complete
    register is what somebody signs.
  - `guideline.md.j2` and `guideline.html.j2` render the same sections in the
    same order. §14's acceptance compares them.
  - The draft watermark is not decoration. §14: "a draft claims register must
    not be able to circulate as a legal sign-off record."
  - A line that ends in `{% endif %}` or `{% endfor %}` must be followed by
    `{{ "" }}`. `trim_blocks` eats the newline after a block tag, so without it
    the next line joins this one — and when the next line is `---`, markdown
    reads the pair as a setext heading and the separator silently becomes a
    title. An empty expression tag is not a block tag, so the newline survives.
#}
